.TH CPL 1 "2026" "Crystal Palace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpl \- linker for post-exploitation and evasion tradecraft security research
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpl
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Crystal Palace is a linker and linker script language specialized to the needs of writing post-exploitation capability and evasion tradecraft.
.PP
The name is inspired by The Crystal Palace, a former cast-iron and glass structure built in London for the Great Exhibition of 1851. At the time, it was the world's largest building. The Crystal Palace adopted a standard size and thread for screws and demonstrated the efficiency gains from building with a standard.
.PP
Like The Crystal Palace, this project aims to demonstrate the efficiency of publishing security research as separate, use-agnostic, and interoperable ground truths.
.PP
The documentation is available at:
.UR https://tradecraftgarden.org/docs.html
.UE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI build " build.spec " "[label.]architecture out.bin " "[A=hex] [%B=val] [@config.spec]"
Run the specified \fI.spec\fR file to assemble a PIC program.
.RS
.TP
.BI @ config.spec
Run a specification file to configure variables.
.TP
.BI \-r " %key=val"
Resolve paths in \fI%key\fR relative to \fB$CWD\fR.
.TP
.BI \-g " out.yar"
Generate Yara rules for this program.
.PP
\fBData Variables ($VARS):\fR
.RS
.TP
.B A=04030201
Places { 0x04, 0x03, 0x02, 0x01 } into \fB$A\fR.
.PP
\fBNote:\fR The '$' prefix is optional to avoid shell escaping.
.PP
\fBWarning:\fR Bytes are written left-to-right. Account for little endian when writing ints, longs, pointers, etc.
.RE
.PP
\fBString Variables (%VARS):\fR
.RS
.TP
.BI %key= value
Sets \fI%key\fR to the literal string "value".
.RE
.RE
.TP
.BI coffparse " file"
Parse COFF and print out how Crystal Palace sees it.
.TP
.BI disassemble " [" \-o " " \fI+opt1,+opt2,...\fR "] [" \-f "] " /path/to/file.o
Disassemble object code from specified COFF file.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " +opt1,+opt2,..."
Apply BTF +options to program.
.TP
.B \-f
Show Iced instruction forms (e.g., PUSH r64) with instructions.
.PP
\fBBTF Options (for use with -o):\fR
.RS
.TP
.B +blockparty
Randomize basic blocks within functions.
.TP
.B +disco
Randomize function order.
.TP
.B +gofirst
Make sure \fBgo()\fR is the first function.
.TP
.B +mutate
Break-up some instructions with constants based on a fixed seed.
.TP
.B +optimize
Trace calls from \fBgo()\fR; remove unused functions.
.TP
.B +regdance
Randomize non-volatile registers in some functions.
.TP
.B +shatter
Randomize basic blocks program wide.
.RE
.RE
.TP
.BI help " [" command "]"
Prints help information for a command.
.TP
.BI info " file.spec"
Print \fI.spec\fR meta-information.
.TP
.BI link " loader.spec " "file.dll|file.o out.bin " "[A=hex] [%B=val] [@config.spec]"
Apply the specified \fI.spec\fR file to build a PIC DLL or COFF loader for file. Arguments are identical to \fBbuild\fR.
.TP
.BI server " [" \-p " " \fIport\fR "]"
Start the Crystal Palace JSON-over-HTTP sidecar service.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Set the listening port.
.RE
